":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-11T03:25:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T21:30:00Z","closed_at":"2026-05-20T19:38:37Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in `4.4.1.stable`, `4.5.dev3`\n**NOT** reproducible in `4.3.stable`\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you type something in the filter bar of the scene tree, and you have a tool script that adds/removes nodes in the scene, sometimes it will cause the scene tree to erroneously rearrange its contents. The nature of this rearrangement ranges from items disappearing/reappearing to items moving back and forth between two different locations, or some combination of the two. Sometimes it will happen one time, and sometimes it will keep repeating.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8835ee24-d9ae-4bb4-bebf-2058595cd1b2)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75111258-539a-4892-aba3-b05cd7e90177)\n\nI have tool scripts for spawning effects like clouds in the sky, or wind trails. These nodes are added to the scene, but they're not owned by the scene, so they aren't saved, and they do not even show up in the scene tree. The fact that they are causing the filtered view of scene nodes to change is strange, but also very disruptive. Trying to select things while having a filter active is sometimes like a game of cat-and-mouse.\n\n**EDIT:** The issue seems to only happen if the `Hide Filtered Out Parents` option is enabled.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI do not have a reliable repro yet, but all I know is that the problem goes away if I get rid of the spawning routines in the tool scripts. I could not repro this on a minimal project.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106264/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}